                    <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
                      <div class="w-11 h-11 bg-blue-100 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center shrink-0">
                        <Icon name={item.icon} class="h-5 w-5 text-blue-600" />
                      </div>
                      <div>
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">
                          {item.title}
                        </h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-sm md:text-base">
                          {item.description}
                        </p>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </CardContent>
                </Card>
              ))}
            </div>

            <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-8 text-center text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              <p>
                In short, automation takes scheduling, execution and result-logging, while topic choice, copy quality and audience interaction stay human. If you don’t have ready-to-publish content yet, AsreSEO <a href="/services/content/" class="text-blue-700 font-semibold underline hover:no-underline">content services</a> cover that link of the chain too.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- How the content cycle automation works -->
        <section class="section-padding bg-linear-to-br from-slate-50 to-indigo-50">
          <div class="container-custom max-w-5xl">
            <div class="text-center mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
                How Does <span class="gradient-text">Content Cycle</span> Automation Work?
              </h2>
              <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mx-auto">
                The content cycle is a six-stage loop with each item’s status refreshed in its calendar row; the final stage feeds the input of next week’s first.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
              {cycleSteps.map((step, index) => (
                <div class="bg-white/90 rounded-xl shadow-xs p-6 border border-indigo-100">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
                    <span class="w-9 h-9 rounded-full bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold shrink-0">
                      {index + 1}
                    </span>
                    <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">
                      {step.step}
                    </h3>
                  </div>
                  <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-sm md:text-base">
                    {step.desc}
                  </p>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>

            <p class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-8 text-center text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              That closed loop is what separates content-cycle automation from a simple schedule: each piece’s outcome flows back into next week’s plan automatically, and the calendar gets sharper every cycle.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Best site content calendar tool -->
        <section class="section-padding bg-white border-t border-gray-200/60">
          <div class="container-custom max-w-5xl">
            <div class="text-center mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
                The Best <span class="gradient-text">Site Content Calendar</span> Tool
              </h2>
              <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mx-auto">
                The best tool isn’t the priciest one — it’s the one your team actually opens daily. Our three criteria: solid multilingual support, workflow statuses from draft to published, and integration with tools your team already uses.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="overflow-x-auto bg-[#0a0e17] rounded-none border-2 border-white/15">
              <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse text-sm">
                <thead>
                  <tr class="bg-black border-b-2 border-white/20 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[#CCFF00]">
                    <th class="p-4 font-bold">Tool</th>
                    <th class="p-4 font-bold">Best For</th>
                    <th class="p-4 font-bold">Why It Works</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/10">
                  {toolChoices.map((tool) => (
                    <tr class="hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors">
                      <td class="p-4 font-semibold text-white">{tool.name}</td>
                      <td class="p-4 text-slate-300">{tool.best}</td>
                      <td class="p-4 text-slate-400">{tool.why}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <p class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-6 text-center text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              Tool choice is half the job; the other half is its template and rules: fixed table columns, defined statuses per item, and someone owning the weekly update. In AsreSEO projects the calendar is built on your own tooling — or if you have none, we suggest the lightest option that gets the job done.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

              <ServiceBenefits lang="en" title="Why a Professional" titleHighlight="Content Calendar" subtitle="Turning content into your business’s strategic asset" benefits={benefits} />

        <!-- Workflow Section -->
        <section class="section-padding bg-linear-to-br from-indigo-50 to-blue-50">
          <div class="container-custom">
            <div class="text-center mb-12">
              <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">
