          <div class="container-custom max-w-5xl">
            <div class="text-center mb-10">
              <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
                A Four-Week <span class="gradient-text">Sample Content Calendar</span>
              </h2>
              <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
                A real channel-and-format mix for a growing business: swap topics for your niche, but keep the channel order and each row’s goal.
              </p>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-3 leading-relaxed">
                The fuller structure and blank template live in our <a href="/blog/content-calendar-guide/" class="text-blue-700 font-semibold underline hover:no-underline">comprehensive content calendar guide</a>; here we fill that structure with a four-week example.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="overflow-x-auto bg-[#0a0e17] rounded-none border-2 border-white/15">
              <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse text-sm">
                <thead>
                  <tr class="bg-black border-b-2 border-white/20 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[#CCFF00]">
                    <th class="p-4 font-bold">Week</th>
                    <th class="p-4 font-bold">Channel</th>
                    <th class="p-4 font-bold">Content Type</th>
                    <th class="p-4 font-bold">Sample Topic</th>
                    <th class="p-4 font-bold">Funnel Goal</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/10">
                  {calendarExample.map((row) => (
                    <tr class="hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors">
                      <td class="p-4 font-mono font-bold text-[#CCFF00] whitespace-nowrap">{row.week}</td>
                      <td class="p-4 font-mono text-xs text-white whitespace-nowrap uppercase">{row.channel}</td>
                      <td class="p-4 text-slate-300">{row.type}</td>
                      <td class="p-4 text-white font-medium">{row.topic}</td>
                      <td class="p-4 text-slate-400 font-mono text-xs">{row.goal}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <p class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-6 text-center text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              This sample deliberately mixes three content kinds: evergreen search articles, interactive social content and emails that bring readers back. Seasonal events and campaigns slot into their week, and if a campaign lands, one promo row joins that week — the rest stays untouched.
